  "body": "Main's pass-start law does not lead a later entry from cleared stock. A new engagement pin measures 332.88 mm2 of uncut stock in its case.\n\n## What the pin does\n\n`outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock` cuts 3 tool radii of floor feed after the first land. The case is a 100 x 40 band of radius 15, the 2D Offset Outside strategy, and a 0.25 mm material grid. The pin checks that no stock is cut by the later entries. On main (`e313aa663`) it fails with 332.88 mm2. The other four engagement pins pass on main.\n\n## Why it is filed\n\nThe pins come from PR #3439. That PR is closed as already implemented by #3353 (`e313aa663`). The split-band, Inside and Auto pins pass and are ported in draft PR #3566. This pin is not ported because it fails on main's law. The result is a behaviour difference, not a compile problem.\n\n## Impact\n\nThe toolpath leaves uncut stock after a cleared part. A user sees the leftover material. The `Auto` pass start is the likely workaround; please confirm it.\n\n## Related\n\n- #3353: the merged pass-start law and its incompleteness guard.\n- #3439: the closed parallel implementation.\n- #3566: the ported engagement pins.\n- #3316: the original issue.\n",
